              "question": "<p>Many viruses ‘hide’ in different portions of the body so that they are safe from immune surveillance. An example of this is the human immunodeficiency virus which hides in the dorsal root ganglion (where the cell bodies of the sensory nerves are)</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n"
